    dcterms:description "Legius syndrome, also known as NF1-like syndrome, is a rare, genetic skin pigmentation disorder characterized by multiple cafC)-au-lait macules with or without axillary or inguinal freckling."^^<http://example.org/invalidDatatype> ;
